<p>Trinity's location along the Highway 31 corridor means a mix of housing types — from older homes near downtown that have weathered decades of Alabama storms to newer properties on the outskirts. Each faces the same fundamental challenge: Morgan County's demanding weather and drainage conditions.</p>

<p>With 55+ inches of rain annually and soil that's heavy with clay, proper gutter systems aren't optional in Trinity. When gutters fail, water pools around foundations instead of draining away. On clay soil, that water doesn't absorb — it spreads and persists, eventually finding its way into basements and crawlspaces.</p>

