<p><strong>What we see in Trinity:</strong></p>

<p><strong>The established core:</strong> Downtown Trinity and the areas near the town center have homes that have been here for generations. These properties often have original gutters — sectional systems with failing seams, hangers that have loosened over decades, and fascia damage hidden behind the installation. When we do replacements here, fascia repair is almost always part of the conversation.</p>

<p><strong>The corridor development:</strong> Highway 31 has brought newer construction to Trinity's edges. These homes are typically 10-20 years old with builder-grade gutters that are starting to show their limitations. Undersized systems, minimal downspouts, cheap hangers — the usual builder shortcuts.</p>

<p><strong>The tree factor:</strong> Trinity has solid tree coverage throughout. Mature oaks, pines, and hardwoods mean continuous debris. Without gutter guards, you're cleaning 3-4 times a year minimum — or watching your gutters overflow because you didn't.</p>

<p>Small towns sometimes feel forgotten by contractors chasing bigger markets. We're based in Hartselle — we understand small-town expectations. When we say we'll be there Tuesday at 9, we're there Tuesday at 9.</p>
