<p>Quick reference for Trinity homeowners:</p>

<p><strong>Older home reality:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Original gutters from the 70s/80s are past their useful life</li>
<li>Check behind gutters for fascia damage — rot hides there</li>
<li>Sectional gutters leak at seams; seamless don't</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Newer homes (under 20 years):</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Builder gutters often undersized for Morgan County rainfall</li>
<li>If overflow happens during heavy rain, problem is capacity</li>
<li>Budget for upgrade within 10-15 years of construction</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Tree debris management:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Heavy tree coverage = gutter guards strongly recommended</li>
<li>Without guards: professional cleaning 2-3 times yearly</li>
<li>Pine needles require guards designed for fine debris</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Seasonal timing:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>March:</strong> Pre-storm season check</li>
<li><strong>November:</strong> Clear fall debris before winter</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Warning signs:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Overflow during moderate rain</li>
<li>Visible sagging or separation</li>
<li>Water staining on siding below roofline</li>
<li>Soft spots when pressing on fascia</li>
